        <h1>LeetCode 2091: Removing Minimum and Maximum From Array (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Given an integer array nums, you must remove both the minimum and maximum elements. You can only remove
                elements from either end of the array. Return the minimum number of deletions required to remove both
                the minimum and maximum elements.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: nums = [2,10,7,5,4,1,8,6]<br>
                Output: 5<br>
                Explanation: The minimum is 1 at index 5 and the maximum is 10 at index 1. The three options are: remove
                both from left (6 deletions), remove both from right (4 deletions), or remove one from each side (2+3=5
                deletions). The minimum is 4.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    int minimumDeletions(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; nums) {
        auto [lo, hi] = minmax_element(nums.begin(), nums.end());
        int p = lo - nums.begin(), q = hi - nums.begin(), len = nums.size();
        if (p &gt; q) swap(p, q);
        return min({p + 1 + len - q, q + 1, len - p});
    }
};</code></pre>
